# ===== RUNTIME TENANT UPLOADS - THE HIGHEST-RISK EXCLUSION IN THIS FILE =====
# wwwroot/uploads is the product's RUNTIME document store, not source. On this machine it already holds real
# business documents that arrived with the CrossBuyDev clone - signed contracts, supplier agreements, invoices,
# a company logo and calendar invitations. Committing them would publish confidential tenant data into git
# history PERMANENTLY: a later `git rm` deletes the file from the tip and leaves every byte in the history any
# clone carries. The directory is recreated by the application at runtime, so ignoring it costs nothing.
# The .gitkeep exception preserves the folder itself for a fresh checkout without admitting any content.
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than /: git cannot re-include a file that sits inside an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY,
# because it never descends into it to see the exception. Excluding the directory's CONTENTS instead leaves the
# directory itself visible, which is what lets the .gitkeep negation below actually take effect.
CrossBuy/wwwroot/uploads/*
**/wwwroot/uploads/*
!**/wwwroot/uploads/.gitkeep

# App_Data/report-assets is the SAME kind of directory and the same risk, one level less obvious.
# ReportAssetOptions.RootPath defaults to App_Data/report-assets resolved against the CONTENT ROOT — which is
# the project directory, i.e. INSIDE this repository — and the Report Studio picker writes real company logos,
# signatures and stamps there at runtime. Deliberately NOT under wwwroot (the static-file middleware knows
# nothing about companies, so a file there would be one guessable URL away from every isolation check), which
# is exactly why the rule above does not already cover it.
CrossBuy/App_Data/*
**/App_Data/*
!**/App_Data/.gitkeep

# ===== Database artifacts =====
# Backups and detached data files are environment state, not source, and are large. The copy-only backup taken
# to clone CrossBuyDB2 -> CrossBuyDev is one of these.
*.bak
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.ndf
*.trn
*.dacpac
*.bacpac

# ===== Preservation / archive binaries =====
# Stage preservation bundles and doc archives duplicate sources that are already tracked in this repository, so
# in git they are dead weight that can never be diffed. Policy is artifact storage, not version control. Their
# .sha256 companions are excluded with them: a checksum for a file the repo does not carry proves nothing.
engineering/preservation/
docs/**/_archive/
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.zip.sha256

# ===== UI-conformance run output =====
# Screenshots and reports PRODUCED by a conformance run are per-machine and per-run. The APPROVED baselines under
# tools/ui-conformance/baseline/ are the opposite - they are the record the gate measures against - so they are
# re-included explicitly and must stay tracked.
tools/ui-conformance/node_modules/
tools/ui-conformance/output/
tools/ui-conformance/screenshots/
tools/ui-conformance/**/*.png
!tools/ui-conformance/baseline/**

# ---- Discovery packages (docs/) -------------------------------------------------------------
# The user-manual discovery carries 541 screenshots at ~57 MB. They are evidence, not source:
# the capture scripts in the package regenerate them, and the ZIP beside the folder holds them.
# Keeping them out of git history keeps the clone light; the documents, catalogues, assets and
# scripts are all committed.
docs/CrossBuy_User_Manual_Discovery/screenshots/
# The same package existed twice on disk while it was being built. Only the named copy is tracked.
docs/user-manual-discovery/
